# Anti-slop design (Signal)

Procedure: `.agent/skills/design-review/SKILL.md`. Spec: `docs/design/design-system.md` (Signal) and `docs/design/ux-blueprint.md`. Principles for design agents: `DESIGN.md` / `PRODUCT.md`.

Every rule is pass/fail. "Make it clean" is not a rule. Slop is the absence of decisions: if nobody can name the decision behind an element and the alternative rejected, it is slop. Swapping one default look for another (banning blue, shipping sage-on-cream) is still a default.

## Tokens (T)

| # | Pass when |
| --- | --- |
| T1 | Every color comes from `packages/ui/src/tokens.css`; no hex, no Tailwind default palette, no shadcn/Nuxt UI default theme. |
| T2 | Brand indigo (`brand-500`) appears as one primary action per view, the active route segment, and focus. One brand fill per view; never a large decorative background. |
| T3 | Fern/saffron/oxblood mean verdict, risk, or status only. Never decoration. |
| T4 | Light and dark both use the token set; dark is cool, not pure black. |
| T5 | Body text contrast ≥ 7:1, secondary ≥ 4.5:1, UI boundaries ≥ 3:1 (token-pair script in CI). |
| T6 | One family: Manrope for UI, display, documents, and data. No second typeface; data uses tabular numerals. |
| T7 | Cards and floating layers use the soft elevation tokens; no ad hoc shadows, glows, or heavy borders. |

## Banned patterns (B), hard fail

| # | Pattern |
| --- | --- |
| B1 | Teal or green accents as brand; gradients, glassmorphism, glows, confetti. |
| B2 | Lucide icons or any second icon set. Phosphor only (Regular; Duotone in empty states/onboarding). |
| B3 | KPI tile grids with icon chips; card-in-card; pastel icon chips. |
| B4 | Sparkle/magic-wand icons to mean "AI". AI is shown by pencil text and proof marks. |
| B5 | Emoji in UI chrome. |
| B6 | Fake precision ("ATS score 97%") or dark patterns; Lens grades are labeled "simulation". |
| B7 | Stock illustrations, 3D blobs, generic hero art. |
| B8 | Status or risk by color alone; must pair color + glyph + word. |

## Layout and hierarchy (H)

| # | Pass when |
| --- | --- |
| H1 | Documents get the widest column (measure 64–72ch); chrome recedes. |
| H2 | Exactly one primary action per view; it sits in the consistent context panel or bottom bar. |
| H3 | The screen reads in grayscale. |
| H4 | Uses the named layouts: Desk sidebar, Reader (list · document · context), Brief, Workbench. No ad-hoc shells. |
| H5 | Usable at 375/820/1440; no horizontal scroll at 375; touch targets ≥ 44px; decisions (triage, approvals, checkpoints) fully possible on phone. |
| H6 | Job titles, company names, errors, and primary labels never truncate; other truncation has a focus-reachable full value. |
| H7 | Loading, empty (with a next step), and error states exist for every data surface. |

## Domain (D)

| # | Pass when |
| --- | --- |
| D1 | Every AI claim, resume line, filled field, and risk flag carries a proof mark that reveals its source. |
| D2 | AI-drafted text is pencil until accepted, then ink. Drafts are never styled like final content. |
| D3 | Progress uses the route line, not a generic bar or kanban-only status. |
| D4 | Risk uses the risk seal (Clear / Caution / Danger) with reasons; "Needs you" and danger are the only loud states. |
| D5 | Dossiers and Tracks use the folder-tab shape in the Track color; Track hues never encode status. |
| D6 | IDs, timestamps, and run logs use tabular numerals in Manrope. No second mono typeface. |

## Copy (C)

| # | Pass when |
| --- | --- |
| C1 | Short labels; full sentences only in the Today brief and explanations. |
| C2 | No hype words, no exclamation marks in system copy, no em dashes (`human-copy.mdc`). |
| C3 | Errors say what happened and what to do next. |
| C4 | Job-search vocabulary, not database vocabulary. |

## Motion (M)

| # | Pass when |
| --- | --- |
| M1 | 160–220ms, ease-out `cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)`, no bounce/overshoot. |
| M2 | Motion is meaningful only: pencil→ink fill, route line advance, Needs-you settle, live-window handoff. |
| M3 | `prefers-reduced-motion` yields instant state changes. |

## Ship criteria

Zero B failures, all T/H/D/C/M pass or have a written exception in the PR, screenshots at 375/820/1440 × light/dark reviewed by `design-reviewer`.
